---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import GstCalculator from '../../components/GstCalculator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="GST Calculator" description="Add GST to a base amount, or extract GST from a GST-inclusive amount — supports all standard Indian GST slabs.">
  <GstCalculator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Two directions of GST calculation</h2>
  <p>"Add GST" starts from a base price and adds tax on top — useful when quoting a price before tax. "Extract GST" does the reverse — useful when you have a final, tax-inclusive price and need to know how much of it was tax, for accounting or invoicing.</p>

  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Supports all standard Indian GST slabs (5%, 12%, 18%, 28%)</li>
    <li>Switches between adding GST and extracting GST from a total</li>
    <li>Instant calculation as you type</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to use this calculator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose "Add GST" or "Extract GST" depending on your starting number.</li>
    <li>Enter the amount and select the applicable GST rate.</li>
    <li>The GST amount and final total appear instantly.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>Adding 18% GST to ₹1,000 gives a GST amount of ₹180 and a total of ₹1,180. Extracting 18% GST from a ₹1,180 total gives back the same ₹180 GST and ₹1,000 base amount.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Applying the rate to the wrong base.</strong> Extracting GST from a total isn't the same as multiplying the total by the rate — it requires dividing by (1 + rate), not just subtracting a flat percentage.</li>
    <li><strong>Mixing up CGST+SGST vs IGST</strong> — this tool calculates the total GST amount; how it's split (intra-state vs inter-state) is a separate accounting classification.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Quoting a price to a customer with GST added</li>
    <li>Reverse-calculating the tax component from a vendor invoice for bookkeeping</li>
    <li>Quick-checking a supplier's GST math before approving a payment</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this handle CGST/SGST/IGST breakdown?</strong> No — it calculates total GST amount only; splitting it between CGST/SGST or IGST depends on whether the transaction is intra-state or inter-state.</p>
  <p><strong>Is this specific to India?</strong> Yes — the slabs (5/12/18/28%) reflect India's GST structure.</p>
</ToolLayout>
